  "auditor": "trapi:gpt-5.6-sol_2026-07-09",
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "Incorporating a modest amount of Mo into a high-entropy alloy enables in situ formation of MoO2 during sliding.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC11124323::web::000::abstract"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Mo addition will reduce both coefficient of friction and wear rate relative to an undoped alloy.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC11124323::web::000::abstract"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The friction and wear reductions will persist over a broad temperature range.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "A controlled Mo fraction added during alloy synthesis will promote MoO2 formation at the friction interface.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC11124323::web::000::abstract"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The sliding interface will develop a thin MoO2 film.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC11124323::web::000::abstract"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The MoO2 film is self-adaptive and layered.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Frictional heating causes Mo in the alloy to oxidize preferentially into MoO2.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC11124323::web::000::abstract"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The MoO2 layer provides an easy-shear interface that lowers interfacial shear stress and friction.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC11124323::web::000::abstract"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Mo addition improves the hardness-toughness balance of the material.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC11124323::web::000::abstract"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The improved hardness and fracture toughness mitigate material removal and reduce wear.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC11124323::web::000::abstract"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The coefficient of friction of the Mo-modified alloy will be lower than that of the untreated alloy.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC11124323::web::000::abstract"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The wear rate of the Mo-modified alloy may decrease by as much as one order of magnitude.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC11124323::web::000::abstract"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The intervention will remain effective whenever operating conditions promote formation and stability of the MoO2 layer.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC11124323::web::000::abstract"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The optimal Mo content and precise improvement magnitude depend on processing and service conditions.",
      "field": "uncertainty",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Mo-modified and Mo-free control samples will be compared using identical dry ball-on-disk tests over multiple temperatures at matched load and speed.",
      "field": "falsification_experiment.design",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Failure to obtain a statistically significant, reproducible reduction in both friction and wear, or failure to detect MoO2 on the wear surface, will falsify the hypothesis.",
